[36m(TaskRunner pid=1047900)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form. Since \(|z| = 4\), we can write \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta)\). Then, we can substitute this into the expression and find the real part.
