[36m(TaskRunner pid=1047900)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1047900)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form. Since \(|z| = 4\), we can write \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1047900)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1047900)[0m Substituting \(z = 4e^{i\theta}\) into the expression, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1047900)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1047900)[0m (75 + 117i)(4e^{i\theta}) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4e^{i\theta}} = 4(75 + 117i)e^{i\theta} + \frac{96 + 144i}{4}e^{-i\theta}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1047900)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1047900)[0m Simplifying further, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1047900)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1047900)[0m 4(75 + 117i)(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4}(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta).
